    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Section 7",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 17a of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting from subsection (1) “an offence against the law of the\nCommonwealth, or o f’ and substituting “a federal offence, or for\nan offence against the law o f’;\n(b) by inserting after subsection (1) the following subsections:\n“(1A) Where:\n(a) a person is convicted of one or more federal offences\nrelating to property, money or both, whose total value does\nnot exceed $2,000; and\n(b) the\nperson\nhas\nnot previously been\nsentenced to\nimprisonment for any federal, State or Territory offence;\nthe court convicting the person must not, unless in the opinion of\nthe court there are exceptional circumstances that warrant it, pass\na sentence of imprisonment for that offence or any of those offences.\n“(IB) For the purpose only, under subsection (lA), of aggregating\nthe value of property or money to which federal offences relate, a\nfederal offence of which a person has not been convicted but which\na court, with the consent of the person charged, has taken into\naccount in passing sentence on the person for another federal\noffence, is to be treated as if it were a federal offence of v hich the\nperson was convicted.”;\n(c) by omitting from subsection (2) “an offence against the law of the\nCommonwealth, or o f’ and substituting “a federal offence, or for\nan offence against the law o f’;\n(d) by omitting subsections (4) and (5) and substituting the following\nsubsection:\n“(4) This section applies subject to any contrary intention in the\nlaw creating the offence.”.\n(2)\nSection 17a of the Principal Act is further amended by omitting\nfrom subsections (1) and (2) “the Australian Capital Territory or” (wherever\noccurring).\nEnforcement of fines etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 17a of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting from subsection (1) “an offence against the law of the\nCommonwealth, or o f’ and substituting “a federal offence, or for\nan offence against the law o f’;\n(b) by inserting after subsection (1) the following subsections:\n“(1A) Where:\n(a) a person is convicted of one or more federal offences\nrelating to property, money or both, whose total value does\nnot exceed $2,000; and\n(b) the\nperson\nhas\nnot previously been\nsentenced to\nimprisonment for any federal, State or Territory offence;\nthe court convicting the person must not, unless in the opinion of\nthe court there are exceptional circumstances that warrant it, pass\na sentence of imprisonment for that offence or any of those offences.\n“(IB) For the purpose only, under subsection (lA), of aggregating\nthe value of property or money to which federal offences relate, a\nfederal offence of which a person has not been convicted but which\na court, with the consent of the person charged, has taken into\naccount in passing sentence on the person for another federal\noffence, is to be treated as if it were a federal offence of v hich the\nperson was convicted.”;\n(c) by omitting from subsection (2) “an offence against the law of the\nCommonwealth, or o f’ and substituting “a federal offence, or for\nan offence against the law o f’;\n(d) by omitting subsections (4) and (5) and substituting the following\nsubsection:\n“(4) This section applies subject to any contrary intention in the\nlaw creating the offence.”.\n(2)\nSection 17a of the Principal Act is further amended by omitting\nfrom subsections (1) and (2) “the Australian Capital Territory or” (wherever\noccurring).\nEnforcement of fines etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-7-norm"
