    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Section",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "20a of the\nPrincipal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting from subsection (1) “whether before or after the\nexpiration of the period specified in the order in accordance with\nsubparagraph 19b (1) (d) (i) or 20 (1) (a) (i)” and substituting\n“before the end of the period specified in the order in accordance\nwith subparagraph 19b (l) (d) (i) or 20 (1) (a) (i) or before the\ncompletion of the sentence or last to be served of the sentences\nimposed under paragraph 20 (1) (b)”;\n(b) by inserting in subsection (5) “or offences” after “the offence”\n(wherever occurring);\n(c) by inserting in subsection (5) “or those offences” after “that offence”\n(wherever occurring);\n(d) by omitting from subparagraph (5) (b) “subsection 20 (1)” and\nsubstituting “paragraph 20 (1) (a)”;\n(e) by adding at the end of subsection (5) the following word and\nparagraph:\n“; or (c) in the case of a person who has been released by an\norder made under paragraph 20 (1) (b):\n(i) revoke the order and deal with the person for\nthe offence or offences in respect of which the\norder was made by ordering that the person be\nimprisoned for that part of each sentence of\nimprisonment fixed under paragraph 20 (1) (b)\nthat the person had not served at the time of\nhis or her release; or\n(ii) take no action.”;\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4. 1990\n(f) by omitting from subsection (6) “the offence” (first occurring) and\nsubstituting “the offence or offences”;\n(g) by omitting paragraphs (6) (c) and (d) and substituting the following\nword and paragraph:\n“; and (c) any other order made in respect of the offence or\noffences.”;\n(h) by inserting in subsections (7) and (8) “or offences” after “the\noffence” (wherever occurring);\n(j) by inserting in subsections (7) and (8) “or those offences” after\n“that offence” (wherever occurring);\n(k) by inserting in subsection (8) “or sentences” after “sentence”\n(wherever occurring).\nAdditional sentencing alternatives",
      "skos:definition": "20a of the\nPrincipal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting from subsection (1) “whether before or after the\nexpiration of the period specified in the order in accordance with\nsubparagraph 19b (1) (d) (i) or 20 (1) (a) (i)” and substituting\n“before the end of the period specified in the order in accordance\nwith subparagraph 19b (l) (d) (i) or 20 (1) (a) (i) or before the\ncompletion of the sentence or last to be served of the sentences\nimposed under paragraph 20 (1) (b)”;\n(b) by inserting in subsection (5) “or offences” after “the offence”\n(wherever occurring);\n(c) by inserting in subsection (5) “or those offences” after “that offence”\n(wherever occurring);\n(d) by omitting from subparagraph (5) (b) “subsection 20 (1)” and\nsubstituting “paragraph 20 (1) (a)”;\n(e) by adding at the end of subsection (5) the following word and\nparagraph:\n“; or (c) in the case of a person who has been released by an\norder made under paragraph 20 (1) (b):\n(i) revoke the order and deal with the person for\nthe offence or offences in respect of which the\norder was made by ordering that the person be\nimprisoned for that part of each sentence of\nimprisonment fixed under paragraph 20 (1) (b)\nthat the person had not served at the time of\nhis or her release; or\n(ii) take no action.”;\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4. 1990\n(f) by omitting from subsection (6) “the offence” (first occurring) and\nsubstituting “the offence or offences”;\n(g) by omitting paragraphs (6) (c) and (d) and substituting the following\nword and paragraph:\n“; and (c) any other order made in respect of the offence or\noffences.”;\n(h) by inserting in subsections (7) and (8) “or offences” after “the\noffence” (wherever occurring);\n(j) by inserting in subsections (7) and (8) “or those offences” after\n“that offence” (wherever occurring);\n(k) by inserting in subsection (8) “or sentences” after “sentence”\n(wherever occurring).\nAdditional sentencing alternatives",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-12-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-12-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "56913d987ce0406df13f6dcbfda1f4249f789b1536c7995acc688bb45431ff94",
      "skos:note": "Amendments to subsections of section 20a of the Principal Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Section",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "20a of the\nPrincipal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting from subsection (1) “whether before or after the\nexpiration of the period specified in the order in accordance with\nsubparagraph 19b (1) (d) (i) or 20 (1) (a) (i)” and substituting\n“before the end of the period specified in the order in accordance\nwith subparagraph 19b (l) (d) (i) or 20 (1) (a) (i) or before the\ncompletion of the sentence or last to be served of the sentences\nimposed under paragraph 20 (1) (b)”;\n(b) by inserting in subsection (5) “or offences” after “the offence”\n(wherever occurring);\n(c) by inserting in subsection (5) “or those offences” after “that offence”\n(wherever occurring);\n(d) by omitting from subparagraph (5) (b) “subsection 20 (1)” and\nsubstituting “paragraph 20 (1) (a)”;\n(e) by adding at the end of subsection (5) the following word and\nparagraph:\n“; or (c) in the case of a person who has been released by an\norder made under paragraph 20 (1) (b):\n(i) revoke the order and deal with the person for\nthe offence or offences in respect of which the\norder was made by ordering that the person be\nimprisoned for that part of each sentence of\nimprisonment fixed under paragraph 20 (1) (b)\nthat the person had not served at the time of\nhis or her release; or\n(ii) take no action.”;\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4. 1990\n(f) by omitting from subsection (6) “the offence” (first occurring) and\nsubstituting “the offence or offences”;\n(g) by omitting paragraphs (6) (c) and (d) and substituting the following\nword and paragraph:\n“; and (c) any other order made in respect of the offence or\noffences.”;\n(h) by inserting in subsections (7) and (8) “or offences” after “the\noffence” (wherever occurring);\n(j) by inserting in subsections (7) and (8) “or those offences” after\n“that offence” (wherever occurring);\n(k) by inserting in subsection (8) “or sentences” after “sentence”\n(wherever occurring).\nAdditional sentencing alternatives"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-12-norm",
