    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-23",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23 Section 23",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-23"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Division:\n\"commencing day” means the day on which section 9 of this Act\ncommences;\n\"Principal Act” has the same meaning as in Division 1 of this Part.\n(2)\nIn this Division, an offence is to be taken to be a federal offence if\nit is an offence that would, if committed on or after the commencing day,\nbe a federal offence for the purposes of Part IB of the Principal Act as\namended by this Act, despite the fact that the offence was committed before\nthe commencing day.\nLicences granted under section 19a of the Principal Act",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Division:\n\"commencing day” means the day on which section 9 of this Act\ncommences;\n\"Principal Act” has the same meaning as in Division 1 of this Part.\n(2)\nIn this Division, an offence is to be taken to be a federal offence if\nit is an offence that would, if committed on or after the commencing day,\nbe a federal offence for the purposes of Part IB of the Principal Act as\namended by this Act, despite the fact that the offence was committed before\nthe commencing day.\nLicences granted under section 19a of the Principal Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-23-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "891e8cdb8ff13b76a2a958de463d5292f7a18174a5878bc2d6ce453c74ea9a4d",
      "skos:note": "Defines terms for Division 1 of Part 1, including commencing day and Principal Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-23",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23 Section 23",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Division:\n\"commencing day” means the day on which section 9 of this Act\ncommences;\n\"Principal Act” has the same meaning as in Division 1 of this Part.\n(2)\nIn this Division, an offence is to be taken to be a federal offence if\nit is an offence that would, if committed on or after the commencing day,\nbe a federal offence for the purposes of Part IB of the Principal Act as\namended by this Act, despite the fact that the offence was committed before\nthe commencing day.\nLicences granted under section 19a of the Principal Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-23-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-23"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24 Any licence granted under section 19a of the Principal Act being a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "licence in force immediately before the commencing day, continues in force,\nwith effect from that commencing day:\n(a) as if it had been granted under section 19ap of the Principal Act\nas amended by this Act; and\n(b) if the period of the licence exceeds 5 years—as if the licence period\nended on the commencing day or 5 years after the licence was\ngranted, whichever happens last.\nLicences revoked or cancelled under section 19a of the Principal Act\nbefore commencing day",
      "skos:definition": "licence in force immediately before the commencing day, continues in force,\nwith effect from that commencing day:\n(a) as if it had been granted under section 19ap of the Principal Act\nas amended by this Act; and\n(b) if the period of the licence exceeds 5 years—as if the licence period\nended on the commencing day or 5 years after the licence was\ngranted, whichever happens last.\nLicences revoked or cancelled under section 19a of the Principal Act\nbefore commencing day",
      "cml:asserts": [
