      "skos:note": "Licence granted under section 19a continues in force with effect from commencing day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 Any licence granted under section 19a of the Principal Act being a",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "licence in force immediately before the commencing day, continues in force,\nwith effect from that commencing day:\n(a) as if it had been granted under section 19ap of the Principal Act\nas amended by this Act; and\n(b) if the period of the licence exceeds 5 years—as if the licence period\nended on the commencing day or 5 years after the licence was\ngranted, whichever happens last.\nLicences revoked or cancelled under section 19a of the Principal Act\nbefore commencing day"
    },
    {
