    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25 Section 25",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect\nof a federal offence has had a licence granted under the Principal Act in\nrespect of that sentence revoked under paragraph 19a (5) (b) of the Principal\nAct before the commencing day, then, whether or not the person has been\narrested and brought before a prescribed authority before that day, the\nPrincipal Act continues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence,\non and after that day, until that sentence is fully served, as if the amendments\nmade by Division 1 of this Part had not been made.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(2)\nWhere a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of\na federal offence has had a licence granted under the Principal Act cancelled\nby a prescribed authority under subsection 19a (7) of the Principal Act\nbefore the commencing day, the Principal Act continues to apply in relation\nto that person and that sentence, on and after that day, until that sentence\nis fully served, as if the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had\nnot been made.\nSentences and orders under subsection 19b (1), 20 (1) or 20ab (1) of the\nPrincipal Act",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect\nof a federal offence has had a licence granted under the Principal Act in\nrespect of that sentence revoked under paragraph 19a (5) (b) of the Principal\nAct before the commencing day, then, whether or not the person has been\narrested and brought before a prescribed authority before that day, the\nPrincipal Act continues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence,\non and after that day, until that sentence is fully served, as if the amendments\nmade by Division 1 of this Part had not been made.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(2)\nWhere a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of\na federal offence has had a licence granted under the Principal Act cancelled\nby a prescribed authority under subsection 19a (7) of the Principal Act\nbefore the commencing day, the Principal Act continues to apply in relation\nto that person and that sentence, on and after that day, until that sentence\nis fully served, as if the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had\nnot been made.\nSentences and orders under subsection 19b (1), 20 (1) or 20ab (1) of the\nPrincipal Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-25-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-25-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6d4857e503e0d1a7f4531f47d1b46514a8fd121bee0dd22368b12d6b348cf335",
      "skos:note": "Continues to apply in relation to a person and sentence after revocation or cancellation of licence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25 Section 25",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect\nof a federal offence has had a licence granted under the Principal Act in\nrespect of that sentence revoked under paragraph 19a (5) (b) of the Principal\nAct before the commencing day, then, whether or not the person has been\narrested and brought before a prescribed authority before that day, the\nPrincipal Act continues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence,\non and after that day, until that sentence is fully served, as if the amendments\nmade by Division 1 of this Part had not been made.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(2)\nWhere a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of\na federal offence has had a licence granted under the Principal Act cancelled\nby a prescribed authority under subsection 19a (7) of the Principal Act\nbefore the commencing day, the Principal Act continues to apply in relation\nto that person and that sentence, on and after that day, until that sentence\nis fully served, as if the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had\nnot been made.\nSentences and orders under subsection 19b (1), 20 (1) or 20ab (1) of the\nPrincipal Act"
    },
