      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3935575e68d496d381b19c50a1c0e9294adcdec3d10b1d5ae630f4cc5b293cae",
      "skos:note": "Application for non-parole period in life imprisonment sentence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-28-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28(1) Section 28",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, before the commencing day, a sentence of life\nimprisonment has been imposed on a person in respect of a federal offence,\nthe Attorney-General, the Director of Public Prosecutions or the person\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\nmay, whether or not the person has begun to serve that sentence, on or\nafter that day, apply to the court by which the person was sentenced:\n(a) if the sentence of life imprisonment is the only sentence imposed\non the person for a federal offence, or is the only such sentence the\nterm of which has not been served when the application under this\nsubsection is made—to fix a non-parole period in respect of the\nsentence of life imprisonment; or\n(b) if the sentence of life imprisonment is cumulative on, or concurrent\nor partly concurrent with, another federal sentence of imprisonment\nor other federal sentences of imprisonment imposed on the person,\nbeing a sentence or sentences not yet served when the application\nunder this subsection is made—to fix a single non-parole period in\nrespect of all the sentences."
    },
    {
