    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28(3) Section 28",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-28-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subject to subsection (4), if a non-parole period is fixed as a result\nof an application under paragraph (1) (b), that non-parole period is to be\ntreated as having commenced on the commencement of the first to commence\nof the sentences of imprisonment referred to in that paragraph and is not\nto be such as would render the person concerned eligible to be released on\nparole before:\n(a)\nthe commencing day; or\n(b)\nthe day on which the person would\nhave been eligible for release if\nthe sentence of life imprisonment had not been imposed;\nwhichever is the later.\n(4)\nWhere, in relation to any sentence\nof imprisonment referred to in\nparagraph (1) (b) other than a sentence of life imprisonment, a non-parole\nperiod (in this subsection called a “previous non-parole period”) has been\nfixed but that non-parole period has not been served when the application\nunder subsection (1) is made, the single non-parole period fixed in accordance\nwith that subsection:\n(a) is to be treated as having superseded that previous non-parole\nperiod; and\n(b) is to be treated as having commenced on the commencement of\nthat previous non-parole period; and\n(c) is not to be such as would render the person eligible to be released\non parole before:\n(i) the commencing day; or\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(ii)\nthe day on which that previous non-parole period would\nhave been served;\nwhichever is the later.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Subject to subsection (4), if a non-parole period is fixed as a result\nof an application under paragraph (1) (b), that non-parole period is to be\ntreated as having commenced on the commencement of the first to commence\nof the sentences of imprisonment referred to in that paragraph and is not\nto be such as would render the person concerned eligible to be released on\nparole before:\n(a)\nthe commencing day; or\n(b)\nthe day on which the person would\nhave been eligible for release if\nthe sentence of life imprisonment had not been imposed;\nwhichever is the later.\n(4)\nWhere, in relation to any sentence\nof imprisonment referred to in\nparagraph (1) (b) other than a sentence of life imprisonment, a non-parole\nperiod (in this subsection called a “previous non-parole period”) has been\nfixed but that non-parole period has not been served when the application\nunder subsection (1) is made, the single non-parole period fixed in accordance\nwith that subsection:\n(a) is to be treated as having superseded that previous non-parole\nperiod; and\n(b) is to be treated as having commenced on the commencement of\nthat previous non-parole period; and\n(c) is not to be such as would render the person eligible to be released\non parole before:\n(i) the commencing day; or\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(ii)\nthe day on which that previous non-parole period would\nhave been served;\nwhichever is the later.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28-ss-3-logic-linearlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28-ss-3-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fce85494af7bec1370de2f8c53870970c4a31717cf0d045ff588c5eae8732d10",
      "skos:note": "Non-parole period treatment for fixed sentences"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-28-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28(3) Section 28",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subject to subsection (4), if a non-parole period is fixed as a result\nof an application under paragraph (1) (b), that non-parole period is to be\ntreated as having commenced on the commencement of the first to commence\nof the sentences of imprisonment referred to in that paragraph and is not\nto be such as would render the person concerned eligible to be released on\nparole before:\n(a)\nthe commencing day; or\n(b)\nthe day on which the person would\nhave been eligible for release if\nthe sentence of life imprisonment had not been imposed;\nwhichever is the later.\n(4)\nWhere, in relation to any sentence\nof imprisonment referred to in\nparagraph (1) (b) other than a sentence of life imprisonment, a non-parole\nperiod (in this subsection called a “previous non-parole period”) has been\nfixed but that non-parole period has not been served when the application\nunder subsection (1) is made, the single non-parole period fixed in accordance\nwith that subsection:\n(a) is to be treated as having superseded that previous non-parole\nperiod; and\n(b) is to be treated as having commenced on the commencement of\nthat previous non-parole period; and\n(c) is not to be such as would render the person eligible to be released\non parole before:\n(i) the commencing day; or\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(ii)\nthe day on which that previous non-parole period would\nhave been served;\nwhichever is the later."
    },
