      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Section 5 of the Commonwealth Prisoners Act 1967",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Section 31"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-32",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32 Section 32",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-32"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect\nof a federal offence has had a parole order made under the Commonwealth\nPrisoners Act 1967 in respect of that sentence revoked under paragraph\n5 (5) (b) of that Act, or by operation of subsection 5 (7) of that Act, before\nthe commencing day, then, whether or not the person has been arrested and\nbrought before a prescribed authority before that day, that Act continues to\napply in relation to that person and that sentence on and after that day,\nuntil that sentence is fully served, as if that Act had not been repealed and\nthe amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had not been made.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(2)\nWhere a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of\na federal offence has had a parole order made under the Commonwealth\nPrisoners Act 1967 in respect of that sentence cancelled by a prescribed\nauthority under section 6 of that Act before the commencing day, that Act\ncontinues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence, on and after\nthe commencing day, until that sentence is fully served, as if that Act had\nnot been repealed and the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had\nnot been made.\nApplication of State or Territory remission or reduction laws to certain\nfederal non-parole periods",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect\nof a federal offence has had a parole order made under the Commonwealth\nPrisoners Act 1967 in respect of that sentence revoked under paragraph\n5 (5) (b) of that Act, or by operation of subsection 5 (7) of that Act, before\nthe commencing day, then, whether or not the person has been arrested and\nbrought before a prescribed authority before that day, that Act continues to\napply in relation to that person and that sentence on and after that day,\nuntil that sentence is fully served, as if that Act had not been repealed and\nthe amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had not been made.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(2)\nWhere a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of\na federal offence has had a parole order made under the Commonwealth\nPrisoners Act 1967 in respect of that sentence cancelled by a prescribed\nauthority under section 6 of that Act before the commencing day, that Act\ncontinues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence, on and after\nthe commencing day, until that sentence is fully served, as if that Act had\nnot been repealed and the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had\nnot been made.\nApplication of State or Territory remission or reduction laws to certain\nfederal non-parole periods",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-32-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-32-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-32-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-32-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f2a4ffaf01be77433e5281106bf4a365c4ffb3839c2ff02e471d8e7fc12bde8",
      "skos:note": "Continues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence, on and after the commencing day, until that sentence is fully served."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-32",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32 Section 32",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect\nof a federal offence has had a parole order made under the Commonwealth\nPrisoners Act 1967 in respect of that sentence revoked under paragraph\n5 (5) (b) of that Act, or by operation of subsection 5 (7) of that Act, before\nthe commencing day, then, whether or not the person has been arrested and\nbrought before a prescribed authority before that day, that Act continues to\napply in relation to that person and that sentence on and after that day,\nuntil that sentence is fully served, as if that Act had not been repealed and\nthe amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had not been made.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(2)\nWhere a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of\na federal offence has had a parole order made under the Commonwealth\nPrisoners Act 1967 in respect of that sentence cancelled by a prescribed\nauthority under section 6 of that Act before the commencing day, that Act\ncontinues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence, on and after\nthe commencing day, until that sentence is fully served, as if that Act had\nnot been repealed and the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had\nnot been made.\nApplication of State or Territory remission or reduction laws to certain\nfederal non-parole periods"
    },
