      },
      "cml:premiseText": "An acceptable referee, or any other person, must not knowingly or recklessly omit from an identification reference any matter or thing without which the reference is misleading in a material particular.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "There is an obligation to provide accurate information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-45",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45 Section 45",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-45"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "Section 23 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting\nafter subsection (1) the following subsection:\n“(lA) Where a cash dealer makes or obtains a record of any\ninformation in the course of carrying out a verification procedure\nunder subsection 20 (8), the cash dealer must retain the record for\nthe period of 7 years after the day on which the relevant account is\nclosed.”;\n(b)\nby omitting from paragraph (2) (b) “or”;\n(c)\nby inserting after paragraph (2) (b) the following paragraph:\n“(ba) if the cash dealer does not hold an identification reference\nfor the person at the time when the record is made and the\ncash dealer (whether before or after that time) carries out a\nverification procedure in relation to the person under\nsubsection 20 (8)—retain the record, together with any record\nof information made or obtained in the course of carrying\nout the verification procedure, for the period for which the\nrecord of information must be retained; or”;\n(d) by inserting in paragraph (2) (c) “and paragraph (ba) does not\napply” after “record is made”;\n(e) by inserting in subsection (3) “, (lA)” after “(1)”;\n(f) by inserting in paragraph (4) (b) “or (8)” after “20 (4)”;\n(g) by inserting after subsection (4) the following subsection:\n“(4a) Where:\n(a) a cash dealer makes or obtains a record of any information\nin the course of carrying out a verification procedure under\nsubsection 20 (8); and\n(b) the relevant account is identified, under subsection 20 (4) or\n(8), in a statement in relation to another account with the\ncash dealer;\nsubsection (lA) applies as if the reference to the day on which the\naccount is closed were a reference to the day on which the last of\nthose accounts is closed.”;\n(h) by inserting in subsection (5), (6) and (7) “, (lA)” after “(1)”.\nSecrecy",
      "skos:definition": "Section 23 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting\nafter subsection (1) the following subsection:\n“(lA) Where a cash dealer makes or obtains a record of any\ninformation in the course of carrying out a verification procedure\nunder subsection 20 (8), the cash dealer must retain the record for\nthe period of 7 years after the day on which the relevant account is\nclosed.”;\n(b)\nby omitting from paragraph (2) (b) “or”;\n(c)\nby inserting after paragraph (2) (b) the following paragraph:\n“(ba) if the cash dealer does not hold an identification reference\nfor the person at the time when the record is made and the\ncash dealer (whether before or after that time) carries out a\nverification procedure in relation to the person under\nsubsection 20 (8)—retain the record, together with any record\nof information made or obtained in the course of carrying\nout the verification procedure, for the period for which the\nrecord of information must be retained; or”;\n(d) by inserting in paragraph (2) (c) “and paragraph (ba) does not\napply” after “record is made”;\n(e) by inserting in subsection (3) “, (lA)” after “(1)”;\n(f) by inserting in paragraph (4) (b) “or (8)” after “20 (4)”;\n(g) by inserting after subsection (4) the following subsection:\n“(4a) Where:\n(a) a cash dealer makes or obtains a record of any information\nin the course of carrying out a verification procedure under\nsubsection 20 (8); and\n(b) the relevant account is identified, under subsection 20 (4) or\n(8), in a statement in relation to another account with the\ncash dealer;\nsubsection (lA) applies as if the reference to the day on which the\naccount is closed were a reference to the day on which the last of\nthose accounts is closed.”;\n(h) by inserting in subsection (5), (6) and (7) “, (lA)” after “(1)”.\nSecrecy",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-45-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-45-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5c98286cd4eb03129b6d42006d55ad41da3a8886f219e0b6aeebe036eae95cfb",
      "skos:note": "Cash dealer must retain records for 7 years after account closure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-45",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45 Section 45",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 70,
      "values:originalText": "Section 23 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting\nafter subsection (1) the following subsection:\n“(lA) Where a cash dealer makes or obtains a record of any\ninformation in the course of carrying out a verification procedure\nunder subsection 20 (8), the cash dealer must retain the record for\nthe period of 7 years after the day on which the relevant account is\nclosed.”;\n(b)\nby omitting from paragraph (2) (b) “or”;\n(c)\nby inserting after paragraph (2) (b) the following paragraph:\n“(ba) if the cash dealer does not hold an identification reference\nfor the person at the time when the record is made and the\ncash dealer (whether before or after that time) carries out a\nverification procedure in relation to the person under\nsubsection 20 (8)—retain the record, together with any record\nof information made or obtained in the course of carrying\nout the verification procedure, for the period for which the\nrecord of information must be retained; or”;\n(d) by inserting in paragraph (2) (c) “and paragraph (ba) does not\napply” after “record is made”;\n(e) by inserting in subsection (3) “, (lA)” after “(1)”;\n(f) by inserting in paragraph (4) (b) “or (8)” after “20 (4)”;\n(g) by inserting after subsection (4) the following subsection:\n“(4a) Where:\n(a) a cash dealer makes or obtains a record of any information\nin the course of carrying out a verification procedure under\nsubsection 20 (8); and\n(b) the relevant account is identified, under subsection 20 (4) or\n(8), in a statement in relation to another account with the\ncash dealer;\nsubsection (lA) applies as if the reference to the day on which the\naccount is closed were a reference to the day on which the last of\nthose accounts is closed.”;\n(h) by inserting in subsection (5), (6) and (7) “, (lA)” after “(1)”.\nSecrecy"
    },
    {
