    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-50",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50 Section 50",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-50"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.71",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 33 of the Principal Act is amended by inserting in\nparagraphs (1) (a), (b), (c) and (d) “Australian currency or” before “foreign\ncurrency”.\n(2) Section 33 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting subsection (3) and substituting the following subsections:\n“(3) An officer may, with such assistance as is reasonable and\nnecessary, examine an article which a person has with him or her if\nthe person:\n(a) is about to leave Australia or has arrived in Australia; or\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(b) is about to board or leave, or has boarded or left, any ship\nor aircraft;\nfor the purpose of finding out whether the person has with him or\nher any currency in respect of which a report under section 15 is\nrequired.\n“(3a) A police officer or a customs officer (being an officer in\nrespect of whom a declaration under section 196 of the Customs\nAct 1901 is in force) may, with such assistance as is reasonable and\nnecessary, search a person if:\n(a) the person is about to leave Australia, or has arrived in\nAustralia, or the person is about to board or leave, or has\nboarded or left, any ship or aircraft; and\n(b) the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that there is on\nthe person, or in clothing being worn by the person, currency\nin respect of which a report under section 15 is required;\nfor the purpose of finding out whether the person has with him or\nher any such currency.”;\n(b) by inserting in subsection (4) “or (3a)” after “(3)”;\n(c) by omitting from subsection (5) “(3)” and substituting “(3a)”;\n(d) by inserting in subsection (6) “, (3a)” after “(3)”;\n(e) by inserting after subsection (7) the following subsection:\n“(7a) An officer may, with such assistance as is reasonable and\nnecessary, go onto or enter any prescribed place and examine the\nplace, and any goods found at or in it, for the purpose of finding\nout whether there is at or in the place, or the goods, any currency\nin respect of which a report under section 15 is required.”;\n(f) by inserting in subsection (8) “or (7a)” after “(7)”;\n(g) by inserting in subsection (10) the following definition:\n“ ‘prescribed place’ means:\n(a) a place for the examination of goods on landing, being\na place appointed under section 17 of the Customs\nAct 1901; or\n(b) a warehouse in respect of which a warehouse licence,\nwithin the meaning of Part V of that Act, is in force;\nor\n(c) a port, airport, wharf or boarding station appointed\nunder section 15 of that Act.”.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 33 of the Principal Act is amended by inserting in\nparagraphs (1) (a), (b), (c) and (d) “Australian currency or” before “foreign\ncurrency”.\n(2) Section 33 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting subsection (3) and substituting the following subsections:\n“(3) An officer may, with such assistance as is reasonable and\nnecessary, examine an article which a person has with him or her if\nthe person:\n(a) is about to leave Australia or has arrived in Australia; or\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(b) is about to board or leave, or has boarded or left, any ship\nor aircraft;\nfor the purpose of finding out whether the person has with him or\nher any currency in respect of which a report under section 15 is\nrequired.\n“(3a) A police officer or a customs officer (being an officer in\nrespect of whom a declaration under section 196 of the Customs\nAct 1901 is in force) may, with such assistance as is reasonable and\nnecessary, search a person if:\n(a) the person is about to leave Australia, or has arrived in\nAustralia, or the person is about to board or leave, or has\nboarded or left, any ship or aircraft; and\n(b) the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that there is on\nthe person, or in clothing being worn by the person, currency\nin respect of which a report under section 15 is required;\nfor the purpose of finding out whether the person has with him or\nher any such currency.”;\n(b) by inserting in subsection (4) “or (3a)” after “(3)”;\n(c) by omitting from subsection (5) “(3)” and substituting “(3a)”;\n(d) by inserting in subsection (6) “, (3a)” after “(3)”;\n(e) by inserting after subsection (7) the following subsection:\n“(7a) An officer may, with such assistance as is reasonable and\nnecessary, go onto or enter any prescribed place and examine the\nplace, and any goods found at or in it, for the purpose of finding\nout whether there is at or in the place, or the goods, any currency\nin respect of which a report under section 15 is required.”;\n(f) b",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-50-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-50-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e3657e92462bf2176a2b91e6c7285159a3969157b67b8ff2955121779e634ad0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-50",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50 Section 50",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 71,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 33 of the Principal Act is amended by inserting in\nparagraphs (1) (a), (b), (c) and (d) “Australian currency or” before “foreign\ncurrency”.\n(2) Section 33 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting subsection (3) and substituting the following subsections:\n“(3) An officer may, with such assistance as is reasonable and\nnecessary, examine an article which a person has with him or her if\nthe person:\n(a) is about to leave Australia or has arrived in Australia; or\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n(b) is about to board or leave, or has boarded or left, any ship\nor aircraft;\nfor the purpose of finding out whether the person has with him or\nher any currency in respect of which a report under section 15 is\nrequired.\n“(3a) A police officer or a customs officer (being an officer in\nrespect of whom a declaration under section 196 of the Customs\nAct 1901 is in force) may, with such assistance as is reasonable and\nnecessary, search a person if:\n(a) the person is about to leave Australia, or has arrived in\nAustralia, or the person is about to board or leave, or has\nboarded or left, any ship or aircraft; and\n(b) the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that there is on\nthe person, or in clothing being worn by the person, currency\nin respect of which a report under section 15 is required;\nfor the purpose of finding out whether the person has with him or\nher any such currency.”;\n(b) by inserting in subsection (4) “or (3a)” after “(3)”;\n(c) by omitting from subsection (5) “(3)” and substituting “(3a)”;\n(d) by inserting in subsection (6) “, (3a)” after “(3)”;\n(e) by inserting after subsection (7) the following subsection:\n“(7a) An officer may, with such assistance as is reasonable and\nnecessary, go onto or enter any prescribed place and examine the\nplace, and any goods found at or in it, for the purpose of finding\nout whether there is at or in the place, or the goods, any currency\nin respect of which a report under section 15 is required.”;\n(f) by inserting in subsection (8) “or (7a)” after “(7)”;\n(g) by inserting in subsection (10) the following definition:\n“ ‘prescribed place’ means:\n(a) a place for the examination of goods on landing, being\na place appointed under section 17 of the Customs\nAct 1901; or\n(b) a warehouse in respect of which a warehouse licence,\nwithin the meaning of Part V of that Act, is in force;\nor\n(c) a port, airport, wharf or boarding station appointed\nunder section 15 of that Act.”."
    },
