    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-51",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51 After section 33 of the Principal Act the following section is inserted:",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-51"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "Arrest without warrant\n“33a. (1) Where an officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a\nperson is guilty of an offence against section 15, the officer may arrest the\nperson without warrant.\n“(2) Where an officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a person\nhas assaulted any officer in the execution of that officer’s duties, the first-\nmentioned officer may arrest the person without warrant.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n“(3) A person must not resist, obstruct or prevent the arrest of any\nperson under this section.\nPenalty: $1,000.\n“(4) Where a person is arrested under this section, sections 212 and 213\nof the Customs Act 1901 apply as though the person had been arrested\nunder section 210 of that Act.\n“(5) In this section:\n‘offence against section 15’ and ‘officer’ have the same respective\nmeanings as in section 33.”.",
      "skos:definition": "Arrest without warrant\n“33a. (1) Where an officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a\nperson is guilty of an offence against section 15, the officer may arrest the\nperson without warrant.\n“(2) Where an officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a person\nhas assaulted any officer in the execution of that officer’s duties, the first-\nmentioned officer may arrest the person without warrant.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n“(3) A person must not resist, obstruct or prevent the arrest of any\nperson under this section.\nPenalty: $1,000.\n“(4) Where a person is arrested under this section, sections 212 and 213\nof the Customs Act 1901 apply as though the person had been arrested\nunder section 210 of that Act.\n“(5) In this section:\n‘offence against section 15’ and ‘officer’ have the same respective\nmeanings as in section 33.”.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-51-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-51-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0269127df62ce8dc86e26bccd24a0321a2f1f35d1b6b3d00510cfed581e3ddad",
      "skos:note": "Resisting, obstructing or preventing arrest without warrant is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-51",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51 After section 33 of the Principal Act the following section is inserted:",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "Arrest without warrant\n“33a. (1) Where an officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a\nperson is guilty of an offence against section 15, the officer may arrest the\nperson without warrant.\n“(2) Where an officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a person\nhas assaulted any officer in the execution of that officer’s duties, the first-\nmentioned officer may arrest the person without warrant.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 4, 1990\n“(3) A person must not resist, obstruct or prevent the arrest of any\nperson under this section.\nPenalty: $1,000.\n“(4) Where a person is arrested under this section, sections 212 and 213\nof the Customs Act 1901 apply as though the person had been arrested\nunder section 210 of that Act.\n“(5) In this section:\n‘offence against section 15’ and ‘officer’ have the same respective\nmeanings as in section 33.”."
    },
